From 15afb15b34e01c8c7a3a03a01b1d698e3a83b4a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:56:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/42] host: let a dead guest process's decoders leave the
 seqno wait

The previous change gets a render thread out of a fence or semaphore
wait once its process is dead. A render thread of a multi-threaded
process can also be spinning in VkDecoder for the next sequence number,
which a killed thread of the same process will never submit; only
mDecodersShouldStop ends that spin, and it is set for snapshots and
renderer shutdown only.

Leave the spin when the process is dead, as upstream gfxstream 42a6636b
does. Unlike 42a6636b, RenderThread::main() keeps looping instead of
breaking out: without upstream bc2cb494 ("Replace ASG channel with
stateful members") the address space graphics context hands the render
thread its wakeups through a 4-entry channel and sends Exit into it with
a blocking send() on teardown. A render thread that stopped reading it
could leave that send(), and the guest's close of the ASG fd, blocked
for good. Looping, the thread reads the rest of what the process sent,
skips its Vulkan commands at the seqno check, and exits on Exit as
before.

vk_decoder.cpp is generated; regenerating it drops this change until
the generator has it too.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#40
---
 host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
index c1516256..8a67a21d 100644
--- a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder.cpp
@@ -163,7 +163,8 @@ size_t VkDecoder::Impl::decode(void* buf, size_t len, IOStream* ioStream,
             if (seqnoPtr && !m_forSnapshotLoad) {
                 {
                     while ((seqno - seqnoPtr->load(std::memory_order_seq_cst) != 1)) {
-                        if (shouldExit.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
+                        if (shouldExit.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) ||
+                            (processResources && processResources->isGuestProcessDead())) {
                             GFXSTREAM_WARNING(
                                 "Process=%s is exitting. Skip processing seqno=%d on thread=0x%x.",
                                 processName ? processName : "null", seqno,
